<title>SWITZERLAND: ACI says Memphis top world cargo airport in Jan 97.</title>
<headline>ACI says Memphis top world cargo airport in Jan 97.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Memphis, base of U.S. express freight carrier Federal Express, was the world's busiest cargo airport in January 1997, said Geneva-based Airports Council International (ACI) in a survey of 492 airports worldwide.</p>
<p>The world's 20 busiest cargo airports in January 1997, with the volume they handled and the percentage change over January 1996, were as follows:</p>
<p>    Airport	  Jan 97 tonnage     Pct change</p>
<p>						 from Jan 96</p>
<p>1 (1) Memphis	173,549 tonnes     (up 24.2)</p>
<p>2 (3) Los Angeles  134,314 tonnes     (up 9.9)</p>
<p>3 (7) Hong Kong    129,917 tonnes     (up 20.3)</p>
<p>4 (2) Miami	  127,955 tonnes     (up 1.5)</p>
<p>5 (6) Tokyo Narita 122,992 tonnes     (up 9.9)</p>
<p>6 (5) New York/JFK 120,020 tonnes     (up 7.1)</p>
<p>7 (4) Louisville   114,800 tonnes     (up 0.4)</p>
<p>8 (9) Seoul	  110,894 tonnes     (up 21.4)</p>
<p>9 (8) Frankfurt    110,569 tonnes     (up  3.3)</p>
<p>10 (10) Singapore  103,437 tonnes     (up 15.9)</p>
<p>11 (12) Chicago     99,064 tonnes     (up 18.1)</p>
<p>12 (11) Amsterdam   89,953 tonnes     (up 4.5)</p>
<p>13 (13) Lon Heathrow 87,714 tonnes    (up 5.5)</p>
<p>14 (16) Anchorage   87,665 tonnes     (up 30.7)</p>
<p>15 (15) NY-Newark   79,042 tonnes     (up 11.4)</p>
<p>16 (14) Paris-CDG   75,537 tonnes     (up 4.5)</p>
<p>17 (19) Taipei	65,680 tonnes     (up 18.7)</p>
<p>18 (17) Atlanta     65,020 tonnes     (up 5.9)</p>
<p>19 (18) Dayton	65,008 tonnes     (up 13.1)</p>
<p>20 (20) Dallas/FW   58,878 tonnes     (up 13.6)</p>
<p>-Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel +4 171 542 7706; fax +7706</p>
</text>
